  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2006-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Expanding, \\(x^2 + 2xy + y^2 = x^2 + y^2,\\) so \\(2xy = 0,\\) i.e. \\(xy = 0.\\)\n\nThis is the union of the two coordinate axes, a pair of lines.\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Expand \\((x + y)^2\\) and simplify",
        "The equation reduces to \\(2xy = 0\\)"
      ],
